Hair for the clay hm08 dummy
============================

Official MakeHuman rule (docs):

  Hair is clothes. Same MHCLO pipeline as outfits, stored in data/hair,
  fitted to the basemesh helper named helper-hair.

  https://static.makehumancommunity.org/makehuman/docs/hairstyles_and_clothes.html
  https://static.makehumancommunity.org/assets/creatingassets/faq/how_can_i_create_hair.html

Core MakeHuman does not ship hairstyles (only "None"). Styles come from
community packs such as hair01 (CC0) on files.makehumancommunity.org.

These OBJ files are shells built from the helper-hair cage already inside
models/base.obj (MakeHuman hm08, CC0). They are placeholders you can replace
with a fitted community MHCLO/OBJ listed in web/parts/hair.json.
